        {
          "name": "All-Out Attacker",
          "pokemon": "Lopunny",
          "shiny": false,
          "gender": "DC",
          "levels": [],
          "description": "<p><a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/lopunny-mega/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Mega Lopunny</a> is the best Mega Evolution available for Normal teams due to its blistering Speed tier, great offensive prowess, and unique ability in Scrappy. Fake Out lets Mega Lopunny serve as an exceptional revenge killer, dealing with worn down foes like <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/meowscarada/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Meowscarada</a>, <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/barraskewda/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Barraskewda</a>, and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/raichu-alola/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Alolan Raichu</a>. It also puts Pokemon like <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/keldeo/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Keldeo</a>, <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/cinderace/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Cinderace</a>, and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/tapu-koko/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Tapu Koko</a> in range of its other attacks safely. With Scrappy, Close Combat notably lets Mega Lopunny take on threats like <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/sableye-mega/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Mega Sableye</a>, <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/aegislash/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Aegislash</a>, and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/gholdengo/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Gholdengo</a>, threatening the defensive cores of Dark and Steel teams. U-turn enables Mega Lopunny to work as a potent offensive pivot, escaping unfavorable situations against walls like <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/slowbro/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Slowbro</a> and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/venusaur-mega/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Mega Venusaur</a> while keeping momentum. Triple Axel threatens common switch-ins such as <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/gliscor/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Gliscor</a> and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/mandibuzz/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Mandibuzz</a>, while Return is Mega Lopunny's hardest-hitting move against most Psychic- and Fairy-types, such as <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/tapu-lele/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Tapu Lele</a> and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/iron-valiant/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Iron Valiant</a>. <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/blissey/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Blissey</a> is a great teammate, taking on the likes of <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/volcarona/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Volcarona</a> and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/zapdos/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Zapdos</a> thanks to its bulk while offering support in the form of Stealth Rock, Toxic, and Teleport. <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/staraptor/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Staraptor</a> switches into Fighting-type attacks from Pokemon like <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/great-tusk/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Great Tusk</a>, <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/buzzwole/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Buzzwole</a>, and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/tapu-bulu/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Tapu Bulu</a>, and its access to Defog and U-turn also prolongs Mega Lopunny's longevity and lets it switch in unscathed. Special attackers like <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/zoroark-hisui/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Hisuian Zoroark</a> and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/porygon-z/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Porygon-Z</a> are able to break past physical walls Mega Lopunny can't, like <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/skeledirge/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Skeledirge</a>, <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/corviknight/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Corviknight</a>, and Slowbro. Hisuian Zoroark also prevents Fighting-types from spamming their STAB moves aimed at Mega Lopunny.</p>",
